<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I94d7e0b00bf7e7da8dc59f299e41b72e8fcb64f4" commit="9192c363bb20c58baf9a9a41424c2fa519878ecb" commit_message="glados: disable power rails in sleep path  For the rails controllable by the host processor through gpios turn them off in the sleep paths. The result is that S3 and S5 will turn off those rails.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47228 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados. Suspended and resumed.  Change-Id: I94d7e0b00bf7e7da8dc59f299e41b72e8fcb64f4 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312320 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312320" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/20/312320/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ife0e2fb11373dd129e20b914b45cd5b56c3493f7" commit="b7c394766fabde28b95beb8745ee4735958331c9" commit_message="chell: disable power rails in sleep path  For the rails controllable by the host processor through gpios turn them off in the sleep paths. The result is that S3 and S5 will turn off those rails.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47228 BRANCH=None TEST=Built for chell.  Change-Id: Ife0e2fb11373dd129e20b914b45cd5b56c3493f7 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312321 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312321" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/21/312321/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I6cfc1ba921d6f1a9a8fdceba1e387e0eedafca89" commit="ac18e70ddcda3342550a905e52514d43639040d5" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Allow disk-based swap files  By default, the Chromium OS kernel allows swapping only to zram devices (for details see commit acc9d0ae7b). But using disk-based files as swap devices is required for machines that have a tiny amount of memory.  This patch introduces a kernel config option (CONFIG_DISK_BASED_SWAP) and a sysctl variable (disk_based_swap) to allow disk-based files as swap devices.  To minimize exposure, CONFIG_DISK_BASED_SWAP is set to N and disk_based_swap is set to 0 by default.  BUG=b:25356904 TEST=Wrote a test program that grows incrementally to a size larger than      system memory, causing paging and swapping.  Verfied that data      pages of the test program were written to the disk-based swap device.  Change-Id: I6cfc1ba921d6f1a9a8fdceba1e387e0eedafca89 Signed-off-by: Saied Kazemi &lt;saied@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311795 Reviewed-by: Aditya Kali &lt;adityakali@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Filipe Brandenburger &lt;filbranden@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311795" owner_email="saied@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/95/311795/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I2e94ff67056b4d3fca795e161d4d49b514f49cf9" commit="f9d1999a7e8fbd7a68c8a229bd5da3ff14270774" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue/mt8173: Use struct device *  The fact that mtk_mfg is a platform device shouldn't really matter except during probe.  Use struct device rather than struct platform_device elsewhere, and use the helper dev_get_platdata() to extract our mtk_mfg data from the device.  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47249 TEST=build &amp; sanity test webgl on oak-rev4  Change-Id: I2e94ff67056b4d3fca795e161d4d49b514f49cf9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311925 Commit-Ready: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Tested-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311925" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/25/311925/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3b34ef67c3d6d7e62278bc378475821feb9b9967" commit="90066d0b91165f5b6fb4f964754e2a063ee38496" commit_message="use strict manifests for more repos  None of these repos download files, so should be easy to convert them over to strict manifests.  BUG=chromium:207003 TEST=precq passes  Change-Id: I3b34ef67c3d6d7e62278bc378475821feb9b9967 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312330 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David James &lt;davidjames@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312330" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/30/312330/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I71ba96787e3becf4d145e77244744de71fbabe0d" commit="6c2f5aff5e01e5d2b6fbcad08e1f291b49d9f9b8" commit_message="Adding suspend/resume case to USB tests  BUG=None TEST=Tested locally against lab DUTs  Change-Id: I71ba96787e3becf4d145e77244744de71fbabe0d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312122 Commit-Ready: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sridhar Sonti &lt;sontis@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312122" owner_email="kalin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/22/312122/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ia9804afe8011a915e4bec306e863d34ad7e27be5" commit="3404b907ef09c18f1bdfefac766202e6a44f07b1" commit_message="edid: Use a better mode for 640x480  The hardcoded clock value for 640x480 was 25.175 MHz.  That's a valid clock to use, but is quite hard to make a non-jittery clock from PLLs. It's much easier to make 25.200 MHz, so let's do that.  The difference between the two modes is 59.9 Hz vs. 60 Hz and it seems better to make a non-jittery 60 Hz rather than a very jittery 59.9 Hz.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:46256 TEST=Insignia monitor works, so do others  Change-Id: Ia9804afe8011a915e4bec306e863d34ad7e27be5 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309540 Reviewed-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 7f32c9f460991e5e3b947117d6ae4080e630a532) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309576 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="309576" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/76/309576/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I4b6361877e0576cc4ea2f643f073f1aab660e434" commit="568b30d39e74bc501f29c7d5db3c310997c220a5" commit_message="veyron: Pulse the i2c clock once if sda was low  On one particular TV the TV was holding SDA low when it came up.  It would release the SDA when the SCL went low the first time. Unfortunately the HDMI i2c port wouldn't transmit until the SDA was released.  Let's detect this case and insert a bogus clock pulse to try to get the other side to release SDA.  It's unclear why the kernel doesn't have this problem.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:46256 TEST=Insignia TV works now  Change-Id: I4b6361877e0576cc4ea2f643f073f1aab660e434 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309258 Reviewed-by: Agnes Cheng &lt;agnescheng@google.com&gt; Commit-Queue: Agnes Cheng &lt;agnescheng@google.com&gt; Trybot-Ready: Agnes Cheng &lt;agnescheng@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Agnes Cheng &lt;agnescheng@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309546 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="309546" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/46/309546/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ia72cac7fda2772f26477e43237678fa30feca584" commit="8734be25d686d9ac782519fc2bbdf224758507a5" commit_message="edid: Don't half parse (and wrongly print) more detailed timings  The EDID parsing code continued to update _some_ fields of the output edid but not others if &quot;did_detailed_timing&quot; was already set.  It also then went on to print out this halfway mix of modes each time, despite the fact that it didn't really update everything.  Let's fix that.  We'll reduce code changes by using a temporary copy of data in detailed_block() and then we'll copy it back if we decide we should update.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:46998 TEST=No more bogus printouts  Change-Id: Ia72cac7fda2772f26477e43237678fa30feca584 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309541 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309609 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="309609" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/09/309609/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Ib67735219fd28516857d9b63f1ba156573f1bea3" commit="1600b80cb5762ec7e668711e6fe2d23be5210054" commit_message="edid: Don't set standard timings as supported if they're not  The set to say that a standard timing was supported was not properly in the &quot;if&quot; test.  That meant that even when standard timings weren't supported, we thought that they were.  That had the side effect of never using the detailed mode.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:46998 TEST=Adafruit panel works now  Change-Id: Ib67735219fd28516857d9b63f1ba156573f1bea3 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309521 (cherry picked from commit 4e4c2816e2239299bc02e3a57fb18056db62b56c) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309552 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org